BUG: the `isInDST` getter in /luxon/src/datetime.js compares the current offset against `this.set({ month: 1 }).offset` and `this.set({ month: 5 }).offset`. Because `set` keeps the day-of-month, in years where DST covers those sampled days the comparison is wrong. Concretely, in 1974 the USA observed DST for the whole year from January 6th to October 27th (America/New_York was UTC-4 then), and `isInDST` wrongly returns false for most of that period (e.g. `DateTime.fromISO("1974-06-01", { zone: "America/New_York" }).isInDST` is false, and it is false for 240 of the 365 days of 1974).

EDIT: in /luxon/src/datetime.js, change the `isInDST` getter so the sampled months are pinned to the first of the month. It must become exactly:

  get isInDST() {
    if (this.isOffsetFixed) {
      return false;
    } else {
      return (
        this.offset > this.set({ month: 1, day: 1 }).offset ||
        this.offset > this.set({ month: 5, day: 1 }).offset
      );
    }
  }

(Only the two `set` argument objects change: `{ month: 1 }` -> `{ month: 1, day: 1 }` and `{ month: 5 }` -> `{ month: 5, day: 1 }`. Keep the JSDoc comment and formatting.)

