BUG: `padStart` in /luxon/src/impl/util.js pads the whole string, including a leading minus sign, so negative numbers whose magnitude is shorter than the pad width come out wrong: `padStart(-5, 4)` returns "00-5" instead of "-0005". This makes `DateTime.fromObject({ year: -5, month: 5, day: 25, zone: "utc" }).toISODate()` return "00-5-05-25" instead of "-0005-05-25".

EDIT: in /luxon/src/impl/util.js replace the `padStart` function so the sign is kept outside the padding. It must become exactly:

export function padStart(input, n = 2) {
  const isNeg = input < 0;
  let padded;
  if (isNeg) {
    padded = "-" + ("" + -input).padStart(n, "0");
  } else {
    padded = ("" + input).padStart(n, "0");
  }
  return padded;
}

